From 46d120210cd6b50df5e5c07c21b30a13a21d1cff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 10:40:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 252/255] dos: patch 0252 -- the ISR MIDI replay's default
 per-IRQ budget 256 -> 384

With 0251 skipping OPL writes that do not change their register, the
largest burst the replay has to write in one SB IRQ fell from 416 to 328
on dosags' S8 fixture (room 35 of the 8-bit sound-on gate). At the old
default of 256 that one IRQ still carried 72 writes over to later IRQs,
late -- a phrase start whose notes sound out of step. 384 covers the
measured peak with 17% headroom without going to 512, which only the
unskipped peak (416) would need.

The bound is still what keeps the time spent inside the ISR finite: 384
x one OPL write (2 outportb + 12 status inportb on ISA). That cost has to
be measured on a 486 before this default is trusted there; the hint
SDL_HINT_DOS_MIDI_DEFER_MAX_PER_IRQ (0250) sets it back to 256 at run
time if it is not.

RENUMBERED 2026-09-25 from 0225 to 0252 (the coordinator's SDL block 0250-0259),
so the series sorts after main's SDL 0240. It lands on main ahead of the RTC
pump series (SDL 0230-0237), which re-applies on top. 0225 never landed on
main; its slot is retired on lab/journeys.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Nz9XeKeVG8Ab7dm8esJsMu
---
 src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
index 30e68fd00..802efc09d 100644
--- a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
+++ b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
@@ -1745,7 +1745,11 @@ bool SDL_DOSMidiIsrTickActive(void)
  * SDL_DOSMidiDeferEnable() sees one cached-bool test per IRQ and nothing else.
  */
 #define MIDI_DEFER_QUEUE 8192u             /* entries, power of two */
-#define MIDI_DEFER_MAX_PER_IRQ 256u        /* bound on ISR time per IRQ */
+/* DOS-PORT patch 0252: 256 -> 384. With patch 0251 skipping no-op OPL writes,
+   the largest burst measured (dosags room 35, the S8 fixture) is 328 writes in one
+   IRQ; at 256 that IRQ left 72 writes late. 384 covers it with 17% headroom. The
+   worst case in the ISR is 384 x one OPL write (2 out + 12 status in on ISA). */
+#define MIDI_DEFER_MAX_PER_IRQ 384u        /* bound on ISR time per IRQ */
 #define MIDI_DEFER_SYNC_MAX 1024u          /* bound on a disable's main-thread write-out */
 #define MIDI_DEFER_SYNC_BATCH 32u          /* entries per interrupts-off batch */
 volatile Uint8 g_mdq_kind = 0;             /* 0 off, 1 OPL3, 2 MPU-401 blind direct */
